fix(pip): Publish the G-buffer position for a thermal optic's infrared look

Review follow up on the thermal optic rule. The pack's scope shaders read the G-buffer position
through s_position, which both scope mods bind to $user$generic2 (models_scope_reticle.s). In this
engine that name is the volumetric light buffer (r2_types.h), and the only code that puts the
position there is phase_3DSSReticle(), the fake scope path, which runs when r__3Dfakescope is on -
it is on in the pack's user.ltx, which is why the pack's shading has worked here. The pack's
infrared() thermal look is the one consumer that cannot work without it, so making a thermal optic
depend on the player leaving that option enabled would be a hidden dependency.

A thermal optic now gets the same copy on its own, without the fake scope reticle pass. It is safe
to overwrite because the volumetric buffer is reset every frame (phase_scene_begin clears
m_bHasActiveVolumetric), and it only runs while such an optic is aimed.